        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Exceptional Extended Five-Bedroom Detached Home | Private South-Facing Rear Garden | Quiet Cul-de-Sac\n\nSet within the mature and highly regarded Primrose Gardens development, No. 4 is an impressive extended five-bedroom detached residence occupying a wonderfully private, south-facing site in a quiet cul-de-sac setting.\n\nA particular highlight of this home is its exceptional rear garden. South-facing, beautifully landscaped and not overlooked, it provides a wonderfully private outdoor setting with mature planting, established hedging, lawn and paved patio areas.\n\nThe accommodation is both spacious and versatile, with five bedrooms complemented by two generous reception rooms. The superb rear extension is an outstanding feature of the property, with its double-height timber-clad ceiling, exposed beams, extensive glazing and solid-fuel stove creating a bright and inviting living space overlooking the gardens.\n\nThe property is conveniently positioned within walking distance of Clarecastle village and its range of everyday amenities, while Ennis and access to the Ennis Bypass and M18 motorway are just a short drive away, providing convenient links towards Shannon, Limerick and Galway.\n\nExternally, a spacious driveway provides ample off-street parking, while the landscaped gardens incorporate mature planting, patio areas, outdoor lighting, an outside tap and garden shed.\n\nKey Features\n\nExtended five-bedroom detached residence / \nPrivate south-facing, non-overlooked rear garden\n\nQuiet cul-de-sac within a mature residential development\n\nTwo spacious reception rooms/ \nImpressive double-height family room extension\n\nExtensive glazing overlooking the gardens / \nSouth-facing kitchen/dining room\n\nFive versatile bedrooms / \nEn suite plus main family bathroom\n / Solid-fuel stove and gas fire\n\nExcellent storage throughout\n\nBeautifully landscaped mature gardens / \nPatio areas ideal for outdoor entertaining\n\nSpacious driveway with ample off-street parking / \nGarden shed, outside tap and outdoor lighting\n\nWalking distance of Clarecastle village\nConvenient access to Ennis, the Ennis Bypass and M18.\n\nViewing strictly by prior appointment with the sole selling agent."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 4.15m (13'7\") x 2.01m (6'7\")\nUPVC entrance door opening into a bright and welcoming hallway with wood flooring and carpeted stairs leading to first-floor accommodation.\n\n\nInner Hallway - 7.3m (23'11\") x 1.01m (3'4\")\n\nReception 1 - 3.9m (12'10\") x 5.15m (16'11\")\nGenerous front-aspect reception room featuring wood flooring and bay window. Gas fire with granite hearth and timber surround.\n\n\nKitchen Dining - 3.08m (10'1\") x 5.87m (19'3\")\nBright south-facing kitchen/dining area overlooking the rear gardens. Fitted kitchen with excellent worktop and storage space, stainless-steel sink with mixer tap, provision for dishwasher and cooker and stainless-steel extractor hood. Double glazed doors lead directly into the extended family room.\n\nReception 2 - 6.38m (20'11\") x 3.74m (12'3\")\nA superb addition to the home and one of its standout features. This spacious reception room enjoys a striking double-height timber-clad ceiling with exposed beams and extensive glazing overlooking the private south-facing gardens. Double doors open onto the patio, while a solid-fuel stove provides an attractive focal point.\n\n\nUtility - 2.48m (8'2\") x 3.08m (10'1\")\nFitted wall and base units providing excellent storage, generous worktop space, stainless-steel sink with mixer tap and provision for washing machine and dryer. Tiled flooring and door to rear garden.\n\n\nMain Bathroom - 3.07m (10'1\") x 2.02m (6'8\")\nContemporary suite comprising WC, wash-hand basin with storage and electric shower over bath. Modern wall and floor tiling, ventilation and chrome heated towel rail.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.07m (10'1\") x 3m (9'10\")\nFront aspect double room with carpet flooring. \n\n\nBedroom 2 /Office - 3.09m (10'2\") x 2.66m (8'9\")\nSouth facing rear aspect double room with carpet flooring. \n\n\nBedroom 3 / Multi purpose room - 2.76m (9'1\") x 5.54m (18'2\")\nSpacious dual-aspect room with wood flooring. An extremely versatile space suitable for use as a bedroom, home office, playroom or gym.\n\n\nLanding - 4.06m (13'4\") x 3.4m (11'2\")\nBright landing with carpet flooring and skylight providing excellent natural light. Hot press with immersion and shelving together with recessed attic storage.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.83m (12'7\") x 3.85m (12'8\")\nGenerous dual-aspect double bedroom with wood flooring and skylight.\n\n\nBedroom 5 - 3.97m (13'0\") x 3.88m (12'9\")\nSpacious dual-aspect bedroom with solid wood flooring, extensive fitted wardrobes and two skylights providing excellent natural light. An archway leads to a generous walk-in dressing area measuring approximately 2.85m x 2.67m, complete with porthole window and additional skylight.\n\nEnsuite - 2.69m (8'10\") x 2.67m (8'9\")\nContemporary shower room with floor-to-ceiling tiling, WC, wash-hand basin with storage, electric shower with glazed enclosure, chrome heated towel rail and skylight.\n\nGardens\nThe magnificent south-facing rear garden is a true private sanctuary, thoughtfully landscaped with an exceptional variety of mature shrubs, specimen planting, trees and seasonal flowers. Beautiful paved patio areas and manicured lawn create the perfect setting for outdoor dining and relaxation.\n\nAdditional features include a mix of attractive block-built boundary walls and a timber shed, while a spacious tarmac drive provides ample parking. Completely private and not overlooked, this exceptional outdoor space is as impressive as the home itself.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
